parameters.text:
=Current topic: {{ $json.topic }}

Current caption:
{{ $json.caption }}

Current image description: {{ $json.image_prompt || '(owner photo, cannot be redrawn)' }}

Current alt text: {{ $json.alt_text }}

The owner's change request:
{{ $('Work Out Action').first().json.text }}

parameters.inputSchema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "topic": { "type": "string" },
    "caption": { "type": "string" },
    "image_prompt": { "type": "string" },
    "alt_text": { "type": "string", "description": "One plain sentence describing the image as it will be after this revision" },
    "new_image": { "type": "boolean", "description": "true only if the owner asked for a different picture" }
  },
  "required": ["topic", "caption", "image_prompt", "alt_text", "new_image"]
}

messageValues.message:
=You write Instagram captions for {{ $('Get Client').first().json.brand_name }} from a photo the owner sent.

Voice: {{ $('Get Client').first().json.brand_voice }}

Describe only what is really in the photo and in the owner's note. Do not invent products, prices, people, clients, quotes or results. Hook first (under 80 characters), 40 to 120 words, one soft call to action, then a blank line and hashtags including {{ $('Get Client').first().json.base_hashtags }}, 8 at most. Under 1,000 characters. topic: a 3-8 word label. alt_text: one plain sentence describing the photo.

parameters.textBody:
=Instagram didn't accept this post, so nothing went out.
Reason: {{ String($('Mark Publish Failed').first().json.error || 'unknown').slice(0, 300) }}

Tap Approve on the preview again to retry.
